From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:55:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harnesses): tag Unity Gateway requests with the
 session's labels

Databricks Unity Gateway logs a per-request Databricks-Ai-Gateway-Request-Tags
header (a JSON object of string tags) in the request_tags column of its usage
tracking and inference tables. Omnigent forwarded no session information to
any provider, so gateway usage could not be grouped or joined back to the
session or its labels.

When a harness targets a Databricks Unity Gateway URL, its requests now carry
that header with omnigent_session_id plus the session's user labels.
Omnigent-owned labels (omnigent.*, cost_control.*, omni_project) are skipped,
the encoding is compact ASCII JSON, and labels are dropped in key order past
8 KiB while the session id is always kept. Other gateways and providers never
get the header. OMNIGENT_GATEWAY_REQUEST_TAGS=0 turns it off.

- databricks_ai_gateway: the header, tag builder, opt-out switch and the
  dict / ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS helpers, next to the attribution helpers.
- claude-native: the CLI and runner launch paths append the tags to
  ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS on gateway launches.
- claude-sdk, codex, pi: the runner hands the encoded tags to the harness
  process in OMNIGENT_GATEWAY_REQUEST_TAGS_VALUE (envelope labels, or one
  label fetch for harnesses that may reach a gateway). claude-sdk and pi add
  the header on gateway providers (pi with its $ template escape); Codex
  gateway providers map it through env_http_headers.
- codex-native: the app-server env carries its own session's tags, from the
  runner's launch snapshot or the CLI's session fetch.

Native CLIs and harness processes read the tags at launch, so a label edit
reaches the header after the next launch or respawn.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4bc2be0e9857e5cfabe3cbf23de8ad134b40f3e5)
